  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Casino Swazi. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Swazi Casino is a Royal Casino variant played in Eswatini (formerly Swaziland). Features unique building mechanics where captured cards are kept face up and top cards can be stolen by opponents for builds. Uses numerical values for picture cards (J=11, Q=12, K=13, A=1/14).',
    objective: 'Capture cards from the layout. First player/team to reach target score (usually 11 or 21 points) wins.',
    gameplay: "Captured cards kept face up in single pile. New captures on top. Capturing card must be on top. You can sort captured cards but opponents don't see the order. Partners share a pile in 4-player game. Layout: 4 initial cards, can be captured or added to. Builds: Single build (sum=value) or Augmented build (multiple sets with same value). Build owner must capture it eventually. Turn: Must play exactly one card from hand. Actions (in any order, before/after playing): 1) Capture (chow) - play card to capture matching card(s) or builds, 2) Create single build, 3) Change build value, 4) Create/add to augmented build, 5) Discard to layout. Can only do one of actions 1/3/5 per turn (involve playing card). Can do multiple of actions 2/4 without playing card. Cannot capture directly from opponent's pile, but can use top card in augmented builds. Drifting: Playing a card that could capture but using it in build instead - legal but opponents can insist on capture if you try to leave capturable cards. Capturing card must go on top of pile.",
    keyRules: [
      '2-4 players, 4 in partnerships, anticlockwise',
      'Picture cards have values: J=11, Q=12, K=13, A=1/14',
      'Cut 4 cards for initial layout',
      'All cards dealt to players',
      'Captured cards kept face up in pile',
      'Top card of capture pile can be used by opponents in builds',
      'Must play exactly one card per turn',
      'Single build: sum of cards = value',
      'Augmented build: multiple sets with same value',
      'Build owner must eventually capture it',
      'Drifting allowed (using capturable card in build)',
      "Cannot capture directly from opponent's pile",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2-4 players. 4 players play in fixed partnerships (partners opposite). Play is anticlockwise.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card pack. Card values: 2-10=face value, J=11, Q=12, K=13, A=1 or 14. All picture cards have numerical values (Royal Casino style).',
      equipment: 'Standard deck, score sheet',
      dealing: "Player to dealer's right cuts 4 cards from middle of deck to form initial layout. Dealer deals all cards to players one at a time. First dealer random; deal passes right. If initial layout has 3+ points in scoring cards or 3+ picture cards, reshuffle and recut.",
    },
    turnFlow: "Captured cards kept face up in single pile. New captures on top. Capturing card must be on top. You can sort captured cards but opponents don't see the order. Partners share a pile in 4-player game. Layout: 4 initial cards, can be captured or added to. Builds: Single build (sum=value) or Augmented build (multiple sets with same value). Build owner must capture it eventually. Turn: Must play exactly one card from hand. Actions (in any order, before/after playing): 1) Capture (chow) - play card to capture matching card(s) or builds, 2) Create single build, 3) Change build value, 4) Create/add to augmented build, 5) Discard to layout. Can only do one of actions 1/3/5 per turn (involve playing card). Can do multiple of actions 2/4 without playing card. Cannot capture directly from opponent's pile, but can use top card in augmented builds. Drifting: Playing a card that could capture but using it in build instead - legal but opponents can insist on capture if you try to leave capturable cards. Capturing card must go on top of pile.",
